	I've come across an amusing bug that some people might find
useful. We all know that corpses from mummies and zombies cannot be
sacrificed -- they're too putrid for the gods. But *partly-eaten*
corpses from such creatures *can*! (Whatever flag tells you that the
thing came from undead gets erased when the corpse become partly-eaten.)
So if a bag of tricks or wand of create monster gives you an undead,
simply put the corpse on the altar, get another monster, start to
eat the corpse...
	I'm playing version 3.0 pl7, so perhaps this has already been
fixed.

